column2:
Be silent and restrain your mind, and do not ask;
43	this is the way of the gods who hold Olympus.
44	But you go to bed, and I shall stay behind here,
45	that I may still stir up the maidservants and your mother;
46	and she in her grief will ask me about each thing.

Nurse, why will you tell of them? There is no need.
501	I shall well observe and know each one myself;
502	but keep your word in silence, and leave it to the gods.
